===== 2026-08-14 NebulaGraph upstream version audit =====

Scope
-----
- Question: whether the open-source community or a later public release fixes the
  task-wal memory-growth mechanism identified on NebulaGraph v3.6.
- Read-only source/history/forum audit. No Nebula service was started, and no
  product source or configuration was changed.

Official public version boundary
--------------------------------
- v3.6.0 tag: de9b3ed800a6627d9845e9289b6bbc5b6faf460a
- latest GitHub release: v3.8.0, published 2024-05-17
- v3.8.0 tag: fa928930ab34f150db522933323aa610e54f26e7
- current release-3.8 head: 15fc0b7a12ba69b3977c6f4a9d70d15ec7f98742
- current master head queried on 2026-08-14:
  cdef57e5fd0a972ec9e51d5272638fd772273f46
- No official v3.7.0 tag or release exists in vesoft-inc/nebula.

Byte-level comparison
---------------------
The following official raw source files have identical SHA-256 values across
v3.6.0, v3.8.0, current release-3.8, and current master:

- src/kvstore/raftex/RaftPart.cpp
  3b0c2c1a872f3c7e2ef3420e66bc6bd5d7bdd7ba8871f084e57c7d64375de221
- src/kvstore/wal/AtomicLogBuffer.cpp
  3af5641a37c66d5a80ed27670857c9beb8538a6406ff7fa1bd74ccc4b7a2e47a
- src/kvstore/wal/AtomicLogBuffer.h
  da9731116d69c04cb5800c72ec375fe2ba4164b502b773636639a4feeeac28fd
- src/kvstore/wal/FileBasedWal.cpp
  a25d6cc58f82f1cb15d3e5840e786109f1dcc2de8b77173e5156ebd9f0e0d79f
- src/kvstore/Part.cpp
  d8b4b8bd31ab0c40756f7f3ccc7693f042bffc804b0b90e1c846a712cecf9034
- src/kvstore/RocksEngine.cpp
  ac7b30301a7e5362fb3d4bb04deb1c9ce01b1b74bb5e936a5df9f0873c204536

Consequence
-----------
- sendHeartbeat() still appends an empty NORMAL log whenever replication is not
  in flight; it is not gated by commitInThisTerm_.
- committing that empty log still writes the per-partition RocksDB commit key.
- FileBasedWal still pushes every empty log into AtomicLogBuffer.
- AtomicLogBuffer capacity/dirty-node/reader-based GC behavior is unchanged.
- Therefore the identified empty-log -> RocksDB memtable plus AtomicLogBuffer
  growth mechanism is not fixed by public v3.8.0 or current public master.

Official issue/PR evidence
--------------------------
- https://github.com/vesoft-inc/nebula/issues/6156
  Open as queried on 2026-08-14; no linked branch or pull request. It proposes
  adding commitInThisTerm_ to prevent repeated no-op logs after the leader has
  committed once in the current term. This matches the identified upstream
  trigger but is not a released fix.
- https://github.com/vesoft-inc/nebula/pull/4386
  Merged in 2022 and already present in v3.6. It adds a physical-GC condition for
  oversized AtomicLogBuffer usage caused by large individual logs; it does not
  stop periodic empty logs or RocksDB commit-key writes.
- https://github.com/vesoft-inc/nebula-storage/issues/390
  Historical reader/GC design issue. Current source still links it from a TODO in
  AtomicLogBuffer::releaseRef(), so its closure is not evidence of a full redesign.
- https://discuss.nebula-graph.com.cn/t/topic/14718
  A maintainer said a raft-log-buffer fix might wait for "3.7". The wording was
  tentative; no public v3.7 release or corresponding code change was found, and
  the same key files remain byte-identical through current public master.

Conclusion
----------
- Several unrelated memory-growth bugs have been fixed historically, and PR #4386
  partially mitigated a different large-log AtomicLogBuffer case.
- The exact task-wal mechanism is not fixed in any currently public open-source
  release/branch inspected. Upgrading v3.6 to public v3.8 alone will not remove it.
- This conclusion does not cover private enterprise/internal branches.
